WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Follow the air but keep airflow separate from sound.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.640
For oral speech sounds, the soft palate and pharyngeal

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.320
walls help separate the oral and nasal routes. Incomplete

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.640
closure can allow air to escape through the nose.

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.300
Speech may sound overly nasal and pressure consonants may

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:19.480
sound weak. Nasal sounds normally use the nasal route

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.220
so the goal is not to close it during

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:21.900
every sound.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:27.410
Now separate three observations. Hypernasality is excessive nasal resonance,

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.890
especially on vowels. Nasal emission is air escaping through

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:34.910
the nose during pressure consonants. Compensatory articulation concerns the

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:37.110
place where a sound is produced, such as a

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.550
glottal stop instead of an oral consonant. Hyponasality is

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:43.990
reduced nasal resonance and may suggest obstruction. These are

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.390
different findings even when more than one is present.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.620
Build the evaluation from several kinds of evidence. Ask

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.800
about cleft history, palate surgery, feeding, hearing, speech development,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.560
and the family's concerns. Examine the palate, uvula, visible

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:03.540
throat structures, tongue, and lips. A bifid uvula may

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.240
suggest a submucous cleft, but it does not establish

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:12.740
the diagnosis. The oral examination alone cannot diagnose velopharyngeal

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:17.200
insufficiency. Add connected speech, syllables, pressure -rich sentences, and

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.240
sustained vowels. Nasopharyngoscopy can show closure during speech.

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:27.050
Document structures, movement, resonance, nasal emission, speech production, and

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:31.830
intelligibility. Then match management to the explanation. A structural

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:35.770
problem may need surgery or a prosthetic device. Neuromotor

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.650
dysfunction may require medical evaluation and individualized care. Learned

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.850
compensatory placement and learned phoneme -specific nasal emission may

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.670
respond to speech therapy. The essential distinction is the

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:51.290
cause of the error, not simply whether the speech

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.370
sounds nasal.
